#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/01-iot_Flame_alert_system.rst:49
msgid "2. Configure Blynk"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/01-iot_Flame_alert_system.rst:52
msgid "**2.1 Create template**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/01-iot_Flame_alert_system.rst:54
msgid "Firstly, we need to establish a template on Blynk. Follow the steps below to create a **\"Flame Alert System\"** template."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/01-iot_Flame_alert_system.rst:60
msgid "Ensure that the **HARDWARE** is configured as **ESP8266** and the **CONNECT TYPE** is set to **WiFi**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/01-iot_Flame_alert_system.rst:71
msgid "**2.2 Datastream**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/01-iot_Flame_alert_system.rst:73
msgid "Create a **Datastream** of type **Virtual Pin** in the **Datastream** page to get the value of Flame sensor module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/01-iot_Flame_alert_system.rst:82
msgid "Set the name of the **Virtual Pin** to ``flame_sensor_value``. Set the **DATA TYPE** to **Integer** and MIN and MAX to **0** and **1**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/01-iot_Flame_alert_system.rst:93
msgid "**2.3 Event**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/01-iot_Flame_alert_system.rst:95
msgid "Next, we will create an **event** that logs the detection of flames and sends an email notification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/01-iot_Flame_alert_system.rst:102
msgid "It is recommended to keep it consistent with my settings, otherwise you may need to modify the code to run the project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/01-iot_Flame_alert_system.rst:106
msgid "Set **EVENT NAME** to ``flame_detection_alert``. At the same time, you can customize the content of email sent by setting **DESCRIPTION** for event triggering. You can also set frequency limits for event triggering below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/01-iot_Flame_alert_system.rst:113
msgid "Go to the **Notifications** page and configure email settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/01-iot_Flame_alert_system.rst:124
msgid "**2.4 Web Dashboard**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/01-iot_Flame_alert_system.rst:126
msgid "We also need to set up the **Web Dashboard** to display the sensor data sent from the Uno board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/01-iot_Flame_alert_system.rst:128
msgid "Drag and drop an **Label widget** on the **Web Dashboard** page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/01-iot_Flame_alert_system.rst:134
msgid "In the settings page of the **Label widget**, select **Datastream** as **flame_sensor_value(V0)**. Then set the color of **WIDGET BACKGROUND** to change with the value of data. When the displayed value is 1, it will be shown in green. When the value is 0, it will be shown in red."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/01-iot_Flame_alert_system.rst:150
msgid "**2.5 Save template**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/01-iot_Flame_alert_system.rst:152
msgid "At last, remember to save the template."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/01-iot_Flame_alert_system.rst:158
msgid "In case you need to edit the template, you can click on the edit button in the upper right corner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/01-iot_Flame_alert_system.rst:169
msgid "3. Run the Code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/01-iot_Flame_alert_system.rst:171
msgid "Open the ``01-Flame_alert_system.ino`` file under the path of ``ultimate-sensor-kit\\code\\iot_project_esp01\\wifi\\01-Flame_alert_system``, or copy this code into **Arduino IDE**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/01-iot_Flame_alert_system.rst:179
msgid "Create a Blynk device using the Flame Detection Alert template. Then, replace the ``BLYNK_TEMPLATE_ID``, ``BLYNK_TEMPLATE_NAME``, and ``BLYNK_AUTH_TOKEN`` with your own."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/01-iot_Flame_alert_system.rst:204
msgid "You also need to enter the ``ssid`` and ``password`` of the WiFi you are using."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/01-iot_Flame_alert_system.rst:211
msgid "After selecting the correct board and port, click the **Upload** button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/01-iot_Flame_alert_system.rst:213
msgid "Open the Serial monitor(set baudrate to 115200) and wait for a prompt such as a successful connection to appear."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/01-iot_Flame_alert_system.rst:221
msgid "If the message ``ESP is not responding`` appears when you connect, please follow these steps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/01-iot_Flame_alert_system.rst:223
msgid "Make sure the 9V battery is plugged in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/01-iot_Flame_alert_system.rst:224
msgid "Reset the ESP8266 module by connecting the pin RST to GND for 1 second, then unplug it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/01-iot_Flame_alert_system.rst:225
msgid "Press the reset button on the R4 board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/01-iot_Flame_alert_system.rst:227
msgid "Sometimes, you may need to repeat the above operation 3-5 times, please be patient."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/01-iot_Flame_alert_system.rst:229
msgid "Now, Blynk will show the data read from flame sensor. In the label widget, you can see the value read by the flame sensor. When the displayed value is 1, the background of the label will be shown in green. When the value is 0, the background of the label will be shown in red and Blynk will send you an alert email."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/01-iot_Flame_alert_system.rst:232
msgid "If you want to use Blynk on mobile devices, please refer to :ref:`blynk_mobile`."
msgstr ""

